/docs/generics


Generics - traits that types can carry, for example
volatile<type>
const<type>
A generic is considered a type, so you can do this:
const<volatile<type>>
with progress, there will be more generics.

structure generics

define packed<struct> {
    /-/ blah blah blah
};

define smartpad<struct> {
    /-/ blah blah blah remake
};

packed:
no padding
smartpad:
minimal padding (resolved by the compiler, reorders the variables)

generics are objects which change behavior of compilation or can understand metadata, there are 3 types of generics,

Full generic (Logic + metadata)
logic generic (only logic, like a inline function but called thru ```name;``` not ```name();```, has no arguments, can interact with variables arround if allowed)
meta generic (for example can change from int to f64 and so on)
